WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.267
[spooky music]

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.874
NARRATOR: Area 51 was
built around a dry lake

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.443
bed known as Groom Lake.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.246
It offered obvious advantages.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.647
RAY GOUDEY: Well, we
needed a good place

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:19.452
to land that we could
land any direction,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.887
depending on where
the wind came from.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:24.124
And the round lake
served that purpose.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.093
It was also protected in the
mountain range around it.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.195
So it wasn't very visible.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:36.536
MAN: Smooth as glass,
just unbelievable.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:40.507
I could take that staff car out
there, and as fast as it'd go.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.276
And it wouldn't
even make a bump.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:47.313
RAY GOUDEY: We had a bunch of
trailers for us to live in.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:55.155
And we had a all-purpose
building where you eat.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:59.359
Didn't have TV, didn't
even have a radio.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.796
ED LOVICK: Paradise Ranch
was the first name that

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.064
was given to the establishment.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:09.602
They thought it would soften the
blow of the austerity that was

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.872
attempt to, perhaps,
convince people it wasn't

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.873
quite as bad as it looked.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:21.414
NARRATOR: Area 51 was created
for one top secret project

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:24.717
called Aquatone.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:28.888
In 1955, men from the
CIA, the Air Force,

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:32.525
and a secret division of
Lockheed came to Paradise Ranch

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.461
to begin work.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.496
TONY BEVACQUA: All they
would tell us was we

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.998
had to go for a pressure suit.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:42.435
So we knew it was going
to be high altitude stuff.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:48.208
Your blood boils above 50,000
without having pressurization.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:51.177
So if you were to
lose pressurization,

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.679
just your engine
conk out, and you're

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:56.015
above 50, that suit saves you.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:59.085
MAN: When pilots fly higher
than man has ever flown,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:02.088
equipment changes are necessary.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.123
NARRATOR: In this
declassified footage,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.694
Ray Goudey prepares for
a flight inside Area 51.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.300
The men look like
nothing seen on earth,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:18.104
and rumors about what was
going on inside Area 51

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.673
started to swirl.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.242
TONY BEVACQUA:
[inaudible] I didn't know

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:26.145
what it was until I got there.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:30.283
And wondered what
I got myself into.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.684
NARRATOR: The men
were testing one

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:39.025
of the most important tools of
the Cold War, the U2 spy plane.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.530
TONY BEVACQUA: There
was no trainer.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.964
There was no two seater.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.535
There was no simulator.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.971
NARRATOR: The U2 was equipped
with high resolution cameras

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:56.109
designed to fly at 70,000
feet and take photographs

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.578
from the edge of
the stratosphere.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:02.715
As the Cold War arms race with
the Soviet Union intensified,

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:06.519
the U2 was America's best hope
for tracking their rival's

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:10.189
growing nuclear arsenal
and it put enormous demands

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:13.326
on pilots who had to
breathe pure oxygen

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.261
to survive at such heights.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.398
MAN: Pilots find the confines
of the helmet and face plate

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.733
conducive to claustrophobia.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.236
A number of pilots have been
dropped from the program

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.871
because of this single factor.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.210
NARRATOR: The government's
cover story for the U2

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:35.615
was that it was being
used for weather research.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.251
MAN: If not conventional
aircraft, then,

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.053
what did they see?

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.855
NARRATOR: The U2 cruised
at three times the height

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.592
of regular airliners
and would sometimes

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.759
be glimpsed by civilians.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.361
MAN: I can't be
sure, but I believe

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.297
I saw the sun glinting off
of windows or observation

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.665
portholes of a sort.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.901
NARRATOR: In the mid
1950s, while both

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.338
the Cold War and
America's interest in UFOs

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.039
were at their peak.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:03.076
MAN: I think it was from
outer space, but friendly.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.711
NARRATOR: The silver
colored planes

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.013
sometimes created confusion.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.351
TONY BEVACQUA: It was pure
aluminum, and we said hey,

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.953
we look like a
bright star up there.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.789
NARRATOR: Pilots were
told to deny everything,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.392
even to aircraft controllers.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.461
TONY BEVACQUA: There
were stories about seeing

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.262
something flying way above.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.931
They may have called it in.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:31.237
But they'll still get nothing,
other than evasive stuff.

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:34.474
RAY GOUDEY: If you get up
along the Canadian border,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.645
the ground controller
questioned my altitude.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.847
Actually he was pretty accurate.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.416
And I said, no, you got to
recalibrate your weapon.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:47.987
[laughs] That's not the
altitude we were at.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.357
NARRATOR: By 1957,
unacknowledged U2

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:56.095
flights were the source of half
of all reported UFO sightings.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:59.966
But they were nothing
compared to what would come.

